-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILPre1`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.PreT.eval_le_mg (s : IState HS) (V : Fin HS → ℕ) :
--       ∀ e : Ex HS, (∀ i ∈ e.regs, |s.top i| ≤ V i) → |e.eval s| ≤ mg V e
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, pre-tables (B5), part 1: magnitude bounds for register expressions
--
--   `mg V e`: a crude magnitude bound of the expression `e` when every register `i` it reads holds a
--   value of absolute value `≤ V i`. It dominates every subterm, so `mg V e < 2^B` gives `e.Bnd s B`
--   (`bnd_of_mg`): the cost bounds of all pushes/assignments of the pre-table programs reduce to one
--   numeric inequality per expression.
